---APM-"],["grc","κατ’","κατά","G2596","P- --------"],["grc","ὄνομα.","ὄνομα","G3686","N- ----ASN-"]]},"gl":{"G3588":"the/this/who","G4245":"Elder","G1050":"Gaius","G27":"beloved","G3739":"which","G1473":"I/we","G25":"to love","G1722":"in/on/among","G225":"truth","G4012":"about","G3956":"all","G2172":"to pray/wish for","G4771":"you","G2532":"and","G5198":"be healthy","G2531":"as/just as","G5590":"soul","G5463":"to rejoice","G1063":"for","G3029":"greatly","G2064":"to come/go","G80":"brother","G3140":"to testify","G4043":"to walk","G3186":"greatest","G3778":"this/he/she/it","G3756":"no","G2192":"to have/be","G5479":"joy","G2443":"in order that/to","G191":"to hear","G1699":"mine","G5043":"child","G4103":"faithful","G4160":"do","G1437":"if","G2038":"to work","G1520":"one","G3581":"foreign","G26":"love","G1799":"before","G1577":"assembly","G2573":"well","G4311":"to help on the way","G516":"appropriately","G2316":"God","G5228":"above/for","G3686":"name","G1831":"to go out","G3367":"nothing","G2983":"to take","G575":"away from","G1482":"Gentile-like","G3767":"therefore/then","G3784":"to owe","G5274":"to take up/suppose","G5108":"such as this","G4904":"co-worker","G1096":"to be","G1125":"to write","G5100":"one","G235":"but","G5383":"to love to be first","G846":"it/s/he","G1361":"Diotrephes","G1926":"to welcome","G1223":"through/because of","G5279":"to remind","G2041":"work","G3056":"word","G4190":"evil/bad","G5396":"to talk nonsense","G3361":"not","G714":"be sufficient","G1909":"upon/to/against","G3777":"neither","G1014":"to plan","G2967":"to prevent","G1537":"out from","G1544":"to expel","G3401":"to imitate","G2556":"evil","G18":"good","G15":"to do good","G1510":"to be","G2554":"to do evil/harm","G3708":"see","G1216":"Demetrius","G5259":"by","G1161":"then","G3754":"that","G3141":"testimony","G227":"true","G4183":"much","G2309":"to will/desire","G3188":"ink","G2563":"reed/stick/pen","G1679":"to hope/expect","G2112":"immediately","G4750":"mouth","G4314":"to/with","G2980":"to speak","G1515":"peace","G782":"to pay respects to","G5384":"friendly/friend","G2596":"according to"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",4,null,"challoner","No greater grace. That is, nothing that gives me greater joy and satisfaction. (Challoner)"],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Taking nothing of the Gentiles. These ministers and preachers of the gospel, whom St. John recommends, took care, as St. Paul did, not to take any thing of the Gentiles, to whom they preached, lest they should be thought to preach to get money by it. But he puts Gaius in mind, that by assisting such men, he would become a fellow labourer in the gospel, and have a share in their reward. (Witham)"],["haydock",9,10,"bede","Diotrephes….doth not receive us, nor those we recommend, but prattles and talks against me. We know no more of this man, nor of Demetrius, of whom St. John gives so favourable a character. (Witham) — It seemeth, saith Ven. Bede, that he was an arch heretic, or proud sect master—upomneso. I will rebuke them, and make them known to be wicked. (Ven. Bede)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","This was a very usual salutation among the Jews, by which they wished every possible blessing might come upon their friends they thus saluted. (Menochius)"],["challoner",4,null,"challoner","No greater grace.... that is nothing that gives me greater joy and satisfaction."],["challoner",7,null,"challoner","Taking nothing of the Gentiles.... These ministers of the gospel are commended by St. John, who took nothing from the Gentiles, lest they should seem to preach in order to get money by it."],["challoner",10,null,"challoner","Diotrephes who loveth.... This man seemeth to be in power, but not a friend to the faithful; therefore this part of the letter might be an admonition to him from the apostle."]],"au":{"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"bede":["Bede the Venerable",1,1,735,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#bede"]},"fa":[[11,null,0,"On Monogamy",null,0,220,"And if I glance around at their examples-(examples) of some David heaping up marriages for himself even through sanguinary means, of some Solomon rich in wives as well as in other riches-you are bidden to \"follow the better things; \" and you have withal Joseph but once wedded, and on this score I venture to say better than his father; you have Moses, the intimate eye-witness of God; you have Aaron the chief priest."]],"fau":[["tertullian","Tertullian",0,"ecclesiastical-writer",null,0]],"ftr":[["Ante-Nicene Fathers, vol. 4 (1885)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/anf04"]]}